```java
// Simple Java class - compiled to bytecode
public class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String message = "Hello from JVM";
        System.out.println(message);
    }
}

// After javac compiles this:
// HelloWorld.java → HelloWorld.class (bytecode)

// The .class file contains bytecode like:
// 0: ldc           #2  // String Hello from JVM
// 2: astore_1
// 3: getstatic     #3  // Field java/lang/System.out
// 6: aload_1
// 7: invokevirtual #4  // Method println

// This bytecode runs on ANY JVM:
// java HelloWorld  (on Windows JVM)
// java HelloWorld  (on Linux JVM)
// java HelloWorld  (on Mac JVM)
// Same .class file, different platforms, no recompilation needed
```

